# deepseek41-ud-iq1s.recipe -- DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-1017 from the official release at Unsloth's UD-IQ1_S per-tensor mix:
# routed experts iq1_s / iq2_xxs (gate_up iq1_s in 34 layers and iq2_xxs in 6, down iq1_s in 20 and iq2_xxs in 20),
# attention and shared expert q6_K / q5_K / q8_0, the Engram table iq4_nl, norms and small tensors cast to their stored
# float type, the DSpark drafter's experts kept as the release's MXFP4 (no rule). The `ggml` quantiser runs its
# own searches (llama.cpp's iq1_s/iq2_xxs procedure, ported in Radiance); iq1_s and iq2_xxs need --imatrix. 251.07 GiB.
#
#   data/engram_tables.py <DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-1017 dir> engram-tables.safetensors   (the release ships none)
#   rad-convert <DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-1017 dir> --add engram-tables.safetensors \
#     --recipe data/recipes/deepseek41-ud-iq1s.recipe --imatrix <imatrix.gguf> -o deepseek41-ud-iq1s.rad
#
# The imatrix is Unsloth's with entries for the fused weights added (data/imatrix_merge.py, docs/deepseek41-hf-direct.md). One rule per weight,
# experts collapsed per layer; first match wins.
# PATTERN  QUANTISER  OPTIONS
